From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 19:17:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01149/11171] [outer-loop] Deep Think result + assessment: the
 selection moat has inverted; verifier = training/search-time environment, not
 inference filter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Deep Think's directional verdict (convergent with our 5x-adversarial evidence):
(Q1) selection moat definitively inverted — irreducible verification class is
unbounded deterministic execution, but a sandbox is a zero-margin commodity, not
an AI moat; (Q2) verifier's home is planning but it yields VALIDITY not directional
gradient — applying it to PSPACE search is a dynamics-vs-heuristics category error,
won't crack L4; (Q3) decentralization gap is structural (representational deficit),
resolved via DISTILLATION not inference routing — the verifier is an automated
ground-truth reward engine; (Q4) steelman = discretization/modality mismatch (code
is a leaky abstraction for spatial gestalt). THE judgment: verifier is a
training/search-time ENVIRONMENT, not an inference-time filter; move capital to
search/memory/distillation. Converges with the existing verifier-as-self-
improvement-reward TOP PRIORITY (Sudoku RFT beat gold-SFT). Outer-loop assessment
accepts the directional claims, flags the '100% capital / demote to dumb loop' as
overshoot (the zero-loss safety wrapper is still the shipped trust product), and
marks the modality-mismatch hypothesis as the key open prediction to track.
Priority-shift flagged for OPERATOR review, not auto-applied.

